/* book exam traps: MISRA compliance alone does not give ISO 26262 compliance: MISRA is coding evidence, while ISO 26262 also needs HARA, safety goals, a safety concept, metrics and verification. | ASIL D is the highest level, A the lowest; QM is not "ASIL 0" but means ordinary quality management with no ASIL requirement. | FTTI is not the detection time: it must hold sensing, confirmation, detection and actuation together. | ASIL decomposition does not lower the safety goal: each part keeps the original tag, such as B(D), and independence must be proved. | MISRA C:2012 bans the heap functions of stdlib.h outright (Rule 21.3); "no allocation after start-up" is a deviation some projects write, not the rule. */
