/* book exam traps: V2X is radio communication, not a sensor that measures anything itself; a V2X car still needs radar and cameras, and V2X adds what they cannot see. | V2V, V2I and V2P do not need cellular coverage; only V2N and cloud services stop when there is no tower. | 802.11p and C-V2X are different radios: 802.11p is ad hoc Wi-Fi at 5.9 GHz; C-V2X has a direct sidelink and a network mode. | A signature is not encryption: it proves who sent the message and that it was not changed, but anyone can still read it. | Convert milliseconds to seconds before multiplying by m/s: 100 ms is 0.1 s, so the latency adds 4 m, not 4000 m. */
